                        "entry_id": "9f8dcf62-44b8-3fed-9abf-05d5d89cee81",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een geslacht Octopus van achtarmige inktvissen uit de familie van Octopodidae"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "koppotigen"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a83edde-e139-401c-b0a1-808106af80a9",
                                "sense_id": "7f2a0fdb-0f3f-3c5b-9fcd-1c28166893c6",
                                "text": "Paul de octopus is bij de één beroemd en bij de ander berucht om zijn voetbalvoorspellingen."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8d6693f0-a91b-36a4-84e5-4ed45e2e5af4",
                        "entry_id": "9f8dcf62-44b8-3fed-9abf-05d5d89cee81",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een extra ademhalingsautomaat voor duikers, onderdeel van de duikuitrusting"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1775dc5d-d8be-4ca6-a142-d85a2ac310ce",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f8dcf62-44b8-3fed-9abf-05d5d89cee81",
                        "source_sense_id": "7f2a0fdb-0f3f-3c5b-9fcd-1c28166893c6",
                        "source_sense_description": "achtarmige inktvis",
                        "target_lang_word": "Krake",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Krake",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb720956-f0bb-30fc-989b-880ab1285a10",
                                        "entry_id": "651efa11-f99b-3bea-ab3f-94271d5017ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Meeresbewohner ohne feste Körperform aus der biologischen Gruppe der achtarmigen Tintenfische; Weichtier mit kurzem, sackartigem Körper und langen, um den Mund herum angeordneten Armen mit Saugnäpfen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "620a43f1-9fa8-4183-a7ab-bcf90598e873",
                                                "sense_id": "cb720956-f0bb-30fc-989b-880ab1285a10",
                                                "text": "Der Begriff Tintenfisch ist eine Sammelbezeichnung. Er kennzeichnet in der Klasse der Kopffüßer die Unterklasse, zu der Krake, Kalmar, Sepia und Nautilus gehören."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d5107ba-6882-4707-b7cf-6e3814a77e1f",
                                                "sense_id": "cb720956-f0bb-30fc-989b-880ab1285a10",
                                                "text": "Die acht Fangarme unterscheiden die Gruppe der Kraken von den übrigen zehnarmigen Tintenfischen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff07bf3b-ac13-481f-8596-2a84fda9392a",
                                                "sense_id": "cb720956-f0bb-30fc-989b-880ab1285a10",
                                                "text": "Von großer Bedeutung ist neben der schönen Zeichnung der Kraken die Tatsache, dass der Speichel der Blauring-Kraken hoch giftig ist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13feee9f-0e06-4c6a-bcc0-5562c3c808b9",
                                                "sense_id": "cb720956-f0bb-30fc-989b-880ab1285a10",
                                                "text": "„Der große Krake wartete unten auf Fraß.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbd458d0-81b8-490b-8492-4b488c0a8e95",
                                                "sense_id": "cb720956-f0bb-30fc-989b-880ab1285a10",
                                                "text": "„In den Ruinen zuckten die Schatten wie mondscheue Kraken vor und zurück.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e2d21a4-11dc-4285-9b5f-abea985abd8d",
                                                "sense_id": "cb720956-f0bb-30fc-989b-880ab1285a10",
                                                "text": "„Der eine oder andere kam von der Vorstellung nicht los, riesige Kraken und andere Kopffüßler lauerten ihnen in den Grotten auf, die mit dem Meer in Verbindung standen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb61d175-6dac-3795-8ff8-68338c48c392",
                                        "entry_id": "651efa11-f99b-3bea-ab3f-94271d5017ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "vielarmiges Seeungeheuer"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in der Literatur und in Erzählungen"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4d6b68d-4b3a-4999-b24e-fed7dd218772",
                                                "sense_id": "eb61d175-6dac-3795-8ff8-68338c48c392",
                                                "text": "In ihren Rettungsbooten werden sie Zeuge, wie der Krake das Schiff zerstört."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Krake",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "695915a7-09b9-3fd7-a78b-c97a05421c3c",
                                        "entry_id": "07fc9447-016c-37e6-93a0-1199694a6a3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "deutscher Nachname"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f4c9339-4dd8-4cf7-a6d7-195c5c5cfc20",
                                                "sense_id": "695915a7-09b9-3fd7-a78b-c97a05421c3c",
                                                "text": "Krake kam ganz außer Atem ins Büro."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fde4e27f-6801-48d4-b1b1-9eeee35c8b33",
                                                "sense_id": "695915a7-09b9-3fd7-a78b-c97a05421c3c",
                                                "text": "Die Krake war der Star des Abends."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "819ebe1b-1beb-4226-a4a4-312f5379fda8",
                                                "sense_id": "695915a7-09b9-3fd7-a78b-c97a05421c3c",
                                                "text": "Krakes feiern heute ihren Hochzeitstag."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c4f2d91b-ef72-4d67-97dd-f722aa2a6b65",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f8dcf62-44b8-3fed-9abf-05d5d89cee81",
                        "source_sense_id": "7f2a0fdb-0f3f-3c5b-9fcd-1c28166893c6",
                        "source_sense_description": "achtarmige inktvis",
                        "target_lang_word": "octopus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "octopus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56e1adbd-582c-3603-abaf-ce9ba5186880",
                                        "entry_id": "05f606bf-5e1d-3921-aa62-edd6ec7f2ce3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several marine molluscs of the order Octopoda, having no internal or external protective shell or bone (unlike the nautilus, squid and cuttlefish) and eight arms each covered with suckers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83d044d1-20af-41b2-950f-9ddd0e8215be",
                                                "sense_id": "56e1adbd-582c-3603-abaf-ce9ba5186880",
                                                "text": "Even octopuses without stylets almost certainly retain the molecular machinery necessary to build them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b159be8e-f8a6-420a-8761-3a04b598e29a",
                                                "sense_id": "56e1adbd-582c-3603-abaf-ce9ba5186880",
                                                "text": "In terms of diversity, cephalopods include the egg case making argonauts, shelled nautiluses, venomous blue-ringed octopuses and enigmatic giants like the giant and colossal squid. […] Fossilised ink sacs are more conclusively known from the extinct “soft-bodied” Coleoidea cephalopods in groups Belemitida (including belemnites with bullet-like internal skeletons commonly found as fossils) and Phragmoteuthida as well as from squid, octopus and cuttlefish fossils."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fbe1818-82ad-4ddb-8125-f3eb5f358a14",
                                                "sense_id": "56e1adbd-582c-3603-abaf-ce9ba5186880",
                                                "text": "In one photograph, a teenaged Leah crouches by a tall cylindrical tank containing what she identified to me as a giant Pacific octopus named Pamela. We were pals, she said, in a voice that I thought seemed to strive for offhandedness, did you know they taste with their skin? Octopuses, I mean."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30e3af51-65e4-365b-b90e-4f6a29b218d4",
                                        "entry_id": "05f606bf-5e1d-3921-aa62-edd6ec7f2ce3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mollusc from genus Octopus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "182668c3-e535-38f9-b1e6-93c0c9b9fc14",
                                        "entry_id": "05f606bf-5e1d-3921-aa62-edd6ec7f2ce3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The flesh of these marine molluscs eaten as food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cc8424f-4441-3954-bb49-a31e14853d93",
                                        "entry_id": "05f606bf-5e1d-3921-aa62-edd6ec7f2ce3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An organization that has many powerful branches controlled from the centre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "octopus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2daae10c-c024-31ef-ab9f-750c73e3f8cc",
                                        "entry_id": "640f6f1a-00fc-3a0e-a134-e1e2414cfcb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put (or attempt to put) one's fingers, hands or arms in many things or places at roughly the same time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f8bc819-8c77-4bd1-8859-deb704f7dec6",
                                                "sense_id": "2daae10c-c024-31ef-ab9f-750c73e3f8cc",
                                                "text": "He rises up on his wasted legs, the healer's hands octopussed on his head."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56b5194a-0552-4338-9080-7b9b086c1272",
                                                "sense_id": "2daae10c-c024-31ef-ab9f-750c73e3f8cc",
                                                "text": "A skinny, sauced-looking gent in shorts and baseball cap wandered in through the door, his arms octopussing no less than three pre-teen girls."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "befb0f76-0c05-4ea3-89c6-1c0cc4c42d62",
                                                "sense_id": "2daae10c-c024-31ef-ab9f-750c73e3f8cc",
                                                "text": "I took off my shirt, standing in swim trunks, embarrassed of my tour body, my hands octopussing around the ashamed drink tickets of my gut."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1706812f-bb88-3c57-9c6d-b0c6c0d835e1",
                                        "entry_id": "640f6f1a-00fc-3a0e-a134-e1e2414cfcb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spread out in long arms or legs in many directions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d1cd5e5-158f-4e18-b175-c7d398334f71",
                                                "sense_id": "1706812f-bb88-3c57-9c6d-b0c6c0d835e1",
                                                "text": "The bug-eyed press octopussed to their respective word processors."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f803454-24f4-462f-84a4-b55da477253f",
                                                "sense_id": "1706812f-bb88-3c57-9c6d-b0c6c0d835e1",
                                                "text": "Dirt roads octopussed into the interior, where there were more dried mud and shrivelled crops."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f100f9ec-fed4-4a8e-b8a6-9f637891d526",
                                                "sense_id": "1706812f-bb88-3c57-9c6d-b0c6c0d835e1",
                                                "text": "He had attached three more on so now there were seven legs octopussing out from underneath the chair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e15f399-41c8-4acf-a8a0-8ccc4eacf247",
                                                "sense_id": "1706812f-bb88-3c57-9c6d-b0c6c0d835e1",
                                                "text": "The main house was a sprawling gray two-story structure with breezeways connecting it to the dining hall and another large wing, making it look like it had outgrown itself and octopused to the other spaces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0598143-fbc4-3a81-9238-2b25af9f83d1",
                                        "entry_id": "640f6f1a-00fc-3a0e-a134-e1e2414cfcb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To plug a large number of devices into a single electric outlet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17ba5339-7f1d-469c-8530-3faefdc8d89c",
                                                "sense_id": "c0598143-fbc4-3a81-9238-2b25af9f83d1",
                                                "text": "If they're all for a single indoor tree, caution against \"octopusing\" of cords from other cords, and the use of a number of cords in a single receptacle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57e5b4b6-c3bf-4048-8b1c-9b640e85c639",
                                                "sense_id": "c0598143-fbc4-3a81-9238-2b25af9f83d1",
                                                "text": "By now, the reservation had electricity so THAT had to be octopussed out to the trailers too."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b280323-8c9f-4c0e-95d5-c072363f6a4f",
                                                "sense_id": "c0598143-fbc4-3a81-9238-2b25af9f83d1",
                                                "text": "The three electrical outlets I could see—though located six feet above the ground, beyond all their little reaches—were octopussed with what looked like more plugs than the circuits could handle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b15ee773-333c-4cac-a4e2-5e796c64617f",
                                                "sense_id": "c0598143-fbc4-3a81-9238-2b25af9f83d1",
                                                "text": "It was an eight-channel audio recording snake, a bundled set of cables with eight plugs octopussing out of either end."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c774d907-62bb-32e4-b48b-bfeceaa65b97",
                                        "entry_id": "640f6f1a-00fc-3a0e-a134-e1e2414cfcb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grow in use vastly beyond what was originally intended."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "056ab8da-a318-4074-8c07-3761cba11ccc",
                                                "sense_id": "c774d907-62bb-32e4-b48b-bfeceaa65b97",
                                                "text": "The interlocking business organizations have octopussed beyond all imagining in recent years; they are intermingled with citizens' union-smashing committees and women's strikebreaking “patriotic” groups, such as Neutral Thousands and Women of the Pacific."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47865d60-2542-4cce-9526-74c10ec11378",
                                                "sense_id": "c774d907-62bb-32e4-b48b-bfeceaa65b97",
                                                "text": "The busy man will do two things at once in his office; and with a little forethought he can practise what psychologist Freeman calls \"brain octopussing\" at home, too."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8edc3d5d-31a6-4507-803c-43bd1763881e",
                                                "sense_id": "c774d907-62bb-32e4-b48b-bfeceaa65b97",
                                                "text": "The course of study should be rooted in a survey of the needs of the community and not \"octopussed\" from swivel chair courses of study prepared for other areas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c611d76-1c9d-439b-8a88-a619c7c20db5",
                                                "sense_id": "c774d907-62bb-32e4-b48b-bfeceaa65b97",
                                                "text": "The performance of it, however, did not improve, being octopussed by centuries-old not-to-move bureaucracy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54e9d284-2d5c-4e68-a6e0-0055fca1779d",
                                                "sense_id": "c774d907-62bb-32e4-b48b-bfeceaa65b97",
                                                "text": "Judging by the way that Boots was octopussing himself into the world of the stud farm and mastering the intricacies of thoroughbred financing, he was well on his way to raping Sport of Kings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d54d99cb-32ab-3271-a924-8e96725b5aa6",
                                        "entry_id": "640f6f1a-00fc-3a0e-a134-e1e2414cfcb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hunt and catch octopuses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8abad7c9-b638-4472-b193-497948b54724",
                                                "sense_id": "d54d99cb-32ab-3271-a924-8e96725b5aa6",
                                                "text": "The sport could be called octopusing or octopus hunting— and any number may play. Supposing you catch an octopus, what do you have?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6086e701-62fd-419b-9f4f-9a1a6c0ab937",
                                                "sense_id": "d54d99cb-32ab-3271-a924-8e96725b5aa6",
                                                "text": "CRABBING AND OCTOPUSSING: Use the same method whether you skindive for crabs and octopi or gather them intertidally."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84cd240-c747-4221-bb66-0ce1dcdd9aa2",
                                                "sense_id": "d54d99cb-32ab-3271-a924-8e96725b5aa6",
                                                "text": "The municipal council assigned food quotas to each section and family contributions within sections. People spent the days before the visit fishing, octopusing, digging taro, cooking, and cleaning public spaces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3d6f465-fd9f-3f52-8782-dedf4454d577",
                                        "entry_id": "640f6f1a-00fc-3a0e-a134-e1e2414cfcb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To behave like an octopus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b159cd32-3713-4ec1-bee8-98a1512efcc4",
                                                "sense_id": "a3d6f465-fd9f-3f52-8782-dedf4454d577",
                                                "text": "Night fell especially dark and cold for August, inky blackness tendrilling in, octopussing even the street lamps, now dim with vague form."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ca32feb-3ac8-4765-87e8-c2e70ced158a",
                                                "sense_id": "a3d6f465-fd9f-3f52-8782-dedf4454d577",
                                                "text": "“Strangled in the middle of the night by one of Molly's eight legs.”\n“Mo-om!” Molly kicked Robin in the shins.\n“Owww!” Robin lunged against the door. “I've been octopused!”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ad30c2a-1b90-4aac-a329-51f92c6a8f1d",
                                                "sense_id": "a3d6f465-fd9f-3f52-8782-dedf4454d577",
                                                "text": "It was quite a conincidence for a mechanical sea creature and he was speculating whether it could possibly have been done on purpose when Katsu stole his other sock and flopped on to the floor with an unbiological bang, whereupon it octopused out of the open door and slid down the banister."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "da5ccb75-e669-48a5-8d9b-78ca2b9f1944",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f8dcf62-44b8-3fed-9abf-05d5d89cee81",
                        "source_sense_id": "7f2a0fdb-0f3f-3c5b-9fcd-1c28166893c6",
